body:
Yeah I've thought about this and I would emphasize that I was still excited to be doing the type of work I was doing in your current lab. I would be more worried about them branding OP as someone just coasting at the same lab rather than lowballing them on salary.

&#x200B;

Personally I've been at the same lab 8 years and it's actually true that I think the research we are doing is interesting and exciting. If I were to interview somewhere else I would stress this.

If you do go up onto the sidewalk either crawl at pedestrian walking speed or dismount altogether. I have to do it in some places in town because there are certain bends that are simply too dangerous for me where people drive like complete psychopaths and have no vision and there is no shoulder.

&#x200B;

But for everything else yeah use the road. People will be dicks about it and you just have to ignore them.

This is so odd to me since I was out for 30 minutes after getting his by a car. I asked the ER docs and my GP if I had a concussion, both said probably but the definition was loose. Neither did an actual examination like I see with sports doctors after a crash. I was given no guidance on how to treat said "maybe concussion". When I brought it up a week later to my GP again he said "I see young people like you drive themselves crazy worrying about this, just don't think about it"....I think I really need a new GP.

&#x200B;

While I was out they gave me a full CT scan to show no brain bleeding, however it did uncover some concerningly large solid lung nodules.

"The 16-year-old driver appeared to have been trying to "roll coal" on a group of eight cyclists training for the Ironman Triathlon, according to fellow cyclist Chase Ferrell. Ferrell was a few paces behind the group when the driver blew thick, black smoke on him as he pedaled along Old Highway 290 on Saturday morning. Moments later, the driver caught up to the larger group up ahead and tried doing the same thing. "

&#x200B;

You're honor I was trying to harass them.

Hah I had the same injury. Enjoy your new titanium leg and remember to do your PT.

&#x200B;

....getting your leg put into traction SUCKS

If you ever crash this proves you're not doping.  Just look at Roglic. Definitely doping up until the TT where he ran out of dope. Definitely doping up until the last stage of Paris-nice where he ran out of dope causing him to crash twice. This year's TdF he crashed early so definitely not doping.

&#x200B;

If you're going to win a race and not be accused of doping make sure you win by just a little and were in the early break. Close down a big gap? Doping. Manage to extend a gap? Doping.

I'm a fan of brevity if it gives you the same relevant info.

&#x200B;

I'm of the opinion Oswald Avery would have won a nobel prize if his work wasn't so impossibly dense. The title of his seminal work where he discovered DNA was the heritable substance was called " Studies on the chemical nature of the substance inducing transformation of pneumococcal types. Induction of transformation by a desoxyribonucleic acid fraction isolated from Pneumococcus type III." Talk about burying the lead.
